.TH CTI-DOMAINS 1 "2026-10-12" "cti-agent 1.3" "CTI Fleet Manual"
.SH NAME
cti-domains \- weekly check of the organisation's domains: registrar, DNS, web, TLS and mail records
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cti-domains
.RB [ \-\-inventory
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-state
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-state\-write ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-registrar ]
.RB [ \-\-out
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-text\-out
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-subject\-out
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-csv\-out
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-actions\-out
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-concurrency
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-timeout
.IR DURATION ]
.RB [ \-\-retries
.IR N ]
.PP
.B sudo cti\-agent cti\-domains
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cti-domains
checks every domain in the inventory file and writes a report.
It is normally run by
.BR run\-domains (1)
from
.B cti\-agent\-domains.timer
every Monday at 08:00, and mailed to the security team through
.BR cti\-mailer (1)
.BR \-\-lane\ dom .
.PP
For each domain it checks:
.TP
.B Registrar
Whether the domain is in the GoDaddy account and whether the account holds
domains the inventory does not list; status, expiry (30 and 60 days, worse
with auto-renew off), the transfer lock, and whether the registrar's
nameservers match DNS.
Read-only: one call to
.BR "GET /v1/domains" .
The auth code that authorises a transfer is never requested.
.TP
.B DNS
A and AAAA records, CNAME, and dangling CNAMEs (a name pointing at a target
that no longer resolves, which anyone able to claim the target can take over).
.TP
.B Web
HTTPS and HTTP for the domain and its
.BR www .
name, following redirects: status, final URL, response time. Live means a
2xx or 3xx answer. Parked pages are recognised by lander and for-sale
markers; GoDaddy hosting markers are reported separately as
.IR registrar-hosted ,
because real Website Builder sites carry them too.
When the registrar was consulted and the account and the inventory
disagree, the report opens with
.BR "INVENTORY vs GODADDY" :
the domains in the account but not in
.I domains.txt
(with status, expiry and auto-renew \(em nothing else in the report checks
them), then the domains in
.I domains.txt
that are not in the account (another registrar or account, lapsed, or no
longer ours), then the domains in
.I domains.txt
whose registration was cancelled, expired or transferred out more than 45
days ago. Those are not probed at all, and such registrations that are not
in
.I domains.txt
either are ignored: GoDaddy keeps them in the account listing for years. A
registration that lapsed within 45 days is still checked and reported, as
it may be recoverable. The lead says the counts in one sentence; the subject still
counts them as Medium findings.
.PP
After it comes a
.B WEBSITES
section that answers "which domains have a live site" directly, one group
each for: live website (final host, status, page title), redirects to
another domain, registrar-hosted, parked or for sale, DNS but no working
page, no website, and not checked. The lead says the same in one sentence.
.PP
When any domain's MX is on Proofpoint on Demand (or
.B PROOFPOINT_POD_TENANT
is set), a
.B "PROOFPOINT ON DEMAND"
section follows, from MX and SPF alone:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
.B Not yet on the gateway
(Medium): mail received by another system, named from its MX host -
Microsoft 365 directly, Google Workspace, Mimecast, another gateway, or an
unrecognised host - with how many weeks it has been that way, from the state
file. Usually an acquisition not yet moved.
.IP \(bu 2
.B Another organisation's tenant
(High): MX on pphosted.com with a tenant id that is not ours.
.IP \(bu 2
.B Send route unconfirmed
(Medium): a domain marked
.B send
whose SPF does not authorise Proofpoint, so its outbound mail does not go
through the gateway. Never reported as "does not send": DNS cannot tell.
.IP \(bu 2
.B Leftovers
(Medium): on the gateway, but SPF still authorises another mailbox provider,
or a Google Workspace DKIM key is still published. SaaS senders in SPF and
Microsoft 365's selector1/selector2 keys are expected and not reported.
.RE
.TP
.B TLS
The certificate is fetched and verified separately from whether a page
loaded: verification failures, expiry within 14 or 30 days, issuer and names.
.TP
.B Mail
MX records and whether every MX host resolves; SPF (present, single, not
.BR +all ,
at most 10 DNS lookups); DMARC (present, enforcing,
.BR pct=100 ,
with
.BR rua= );
DKIM keys at the configured selectors, including key size; and the SMTP
greeting and STARTTLS on the first answering MX.
Which rules apply depends on the domain's
.B profile
(below): a sending domain must be able to send; a domain that sends nothing
must say so in DNS
.RB ( "v=spf1 \-all" ,
.BR p=reject ),
and one that publishes senders anyway is reported as a question.
.TP
.B Profiles
The security team's decision chart, one row per profile, chosen by the
inventory markers:
.BR "send receive" :
1, active mail domain;
.BR send :
2, send-only (no MX needed);
.BR receive :
3, receive-only;
no marker: 4/5, no mail at all (null MX preferred);
.BR saas :
6, an application or service sends as it;
.BR unknown :
7, senders not known \(em reported, never tightened;
.BR "send receive legacy" :
8;
.BR "receive legacy" :
9, outbound moved to the main domain.
SPF that is broken (over 10 lookups, several records,
.BR +all )
is row 10: fix it first, and no DMARC enforcement is asked for until then.
.TP
.B DNS changes
The difference between each domain's profile and its DNS, as records for IT.
For rows 3, 4/5 and 9 they are exact:
.B TXT @ v=spf1 \-all
(replacing any other SPF),
.B TXT _dmarc
with
.B p=reject
(existing tags such as
.B rua=
kept,
.B pct=
dropped),
deletion of any DKIM key, and for 4/5 a null MX
.RB ( "MX 0 ." ).
For sending rows the only exact record is a missing DMARC, started at
.B p=none
with
.BR DOMAINS_DMARC_RUA ;
the rest are review items. A failed lookup never produces a change. The
report lists them under DNS CHANGES FOR IT, and
.B \-\-actions\-out
writes them for
.BR cti\-jira (1)
.BR \-\-domains\-actions .
.TP
.B Changes
Nameservers, MX, SPF, DMARC, CNAMEs, live and parked state, certificate
issuer, registrar fields, and any domain that left the account, compared
with the previous run's state file.
.PP
A lookup that fails is reported as
.IR "not checked" ,
never as a missing record, and is never reported as a change.
.PP
.B cti-domains
does not send mail and changes nothing it checks.
.SH OPTIONS
Go's flag syntax: each option may also be written with a single dash
.RB ( \-out ),
and a value may follow
.B =
or a space.
.TP
.BI \-\-inventory " FILE"
The domain inventory: one domain per line, followed by any of the markers
.BR send ,
.BR receive ,
.BR saas ,
.B unknown
and
.B legacy
(space- or comma-separated) that choose its profile,
.B #
for comments. Names are normalised (scheme, path, port and case removed);
lines that are not hostnames, duplicates and unknown markers are listed in
the report under INVENTORY FILE PROBLEMS rather than silently dropped.
Default:\~\fB$DOMAINS_FILE\fR, else \fI/etc/cti\-agent/domains.txt\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-state " FILE"
Last run's observations, read for the week-over-week comparison and then
replaced.
Default:\~\fI$FLEET_HOME/state/domains\-state.json\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-state\-write
Read the state file but do not replace it. Used by
.B run\-domains \-\-dry\-run
so a preview does not become the baseline the next real run compares with.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-registrar
Skip GoDaddy. DNS, web, TLS and mail checks still run; the subject says
.BR "[REGISTRAR NOT CHECKED]" .
.TP
.BI \-\-out " FILE"
Write the HTML report to
.IR FILE ,
mode 0600.
.TP
.BI \-\-text\-out " FILE"
Write the plain-text report to
.IR FILE ,
mode 0600. If neither
.B \-\-out
nor
.B \-\-text\-out
is given, the text report goes to standard output.
.TP
.BI \-\-subject\-out " FILE"
Write the subject line to
.IR FILE ,
so the runner does not probe every domain a second time to build it.
.TP
.BI \-\-actions\-out " FILE"
Write the DNS changes (see DESCRIPTION) as JSON, mode 0600: each change's
domain, profile, record type and host, the value to set, the current value
and why, plus counts and a hash of the list.
.B run\-domains
passes it to
.BR "cti\-jira \-\-domains\-actions" .
Default:\~not written.
.TP
.B \-\-ticket\-slot
Leave an invisible slot beside the DNS changes for
.B \-\-stamp\-ticket
to fill with the lock-down ticket's key, status and link.
.B run\-domains
passes it. Default:\~off.
.TP
.BI \-\-stamp\-ticket " FILE"
Read a
.B cti\-jira \-\-ref\-out
file and stamp its line into the
.B \-\-out
and
.B \-\-text\-out
reports already written, then exit; nothing is probed. The link is included
only if it is an https Jira browse link for that key. A missing or
unreadable
.I FILE
stamps "status unavailable this run"; an action of
.B none
removes the slot.
Default:\~empty.
.TP
.BI \-\-csv\-out " FILE"
Write every probed host as CSV, mode 0600. The first 28 columns are the
original
.B sitecheck.go
columns in its order and under its names; the lane's additions follow.
Cells beginning with
.BR = ,
.BR + ,
.B \-
or
.B @
are prefixed with
.B '
so a spreadsheet does not execute them.
.TP
.BI \-\-concurrency " N"
Domains probed at once.
Default:\~\fB8\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " DURATION"
Timeout for one web request, TLS handshake or SMTP greeting, as a Go
duration
.RB ( 10s ,
.BR 1m ).
Each domain's whole probe is bounded at six times this.
Default:\~\fB10s\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-retries " N"
How many times a web request that got no response at all is repeated. A
response of any status is an answer and is never retried.
Default:\~\fB1\fR.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Read from the process environment, after
.I fleet.env
is loaded (existing environment variables win).
.TP
.B DOMAINS_FILE
Inventory path when
.B \-\-inventory
is not given.
.TP
.B GODADDY_PAT
GoDaddy Personal Access Token, scope
.B domains.domain:read
only. Unset: registrar checks are skipped and the subject says so.
.TP
.B DOMAINS_DNS_SERVERS
DNS servers to ask, as IPs with optional ports, comma- or space-separated.
Empty: the public resolvers 1.1.1.1 and 8.8.8.8, because a box on the
corporate network may resolve the organisation's own domains through an
internal zone without SPF or DMARC.
.B system
uses this host's resolver. The web and SMTP probes connect to the addresses
these servers return.
.TP
.B PROOFPOINT_POD_TENANT
Our Proofpoint on Demand tenant id. Empty: the most common tenant in the
inventory's MX records; with no domain on pphosted.com the gateway section
is off.
.TP
.B DOMAINS_DKIM_SELECTORS
DKIM selectors to probe, comma- or space-separated. Empty: selector1,
selector2, google, default, mail, s1, s2, k1, k2, k3, dkim. A key at any
other selector is invisible to the check.
.TP
.B DOMAINS_DMARC_RUA
When set, every sending domain's DMARC
.B rua=
must include this address. Empty: any
.B rua=
satisfies the check.
.TP
.B DOMAINS_SMTP
.B off
disables the SMTP greeting and STARTTLS probe. When every probe fails to
connect, the report says once that outbound port 25 appears blocked.
.TP
.B DOMAINS_SMTP_PORT
Port for the SMTP probe. Default:\~\fB25\fR.
.TP
.BR FLEET_HOME ", " FLEET_ENV ", " FLEET_ORG
Fleet layout, the
.I fleet.env
path, and the organisation name in the report banner.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/cti\-agent/domains.txt
The inventory. Kept outside the repository, which is public;
.B root:ctiagent
0640.
.TP
.I /etc/cti\-agent/fleet.env
Settings and the GoDaddy token.
.TP
.I /var/lib/cti\-agent/state/domains\-state.json
Last run's observations, 0600. Delete it to start a fresh baseline.
.TP
.I /var/lib/cti\-agent/state/domains\-YYYY\-MM\-DD.{html,txt,csv,subject}
The report files written by
.BR run\-domains ,
0600.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The report was written. A registrar that could not be reached is not a
failure; the report says it was not checked.
.TP
.B 1
Nothing usable was produced: the inventory is missing, unreadable or empty;
.B DOMAINS_DNS_SERVERS
or
.B DOMAINS_SMTP_PORT
is invalid; the state file is corrupt (move it aside to start over); or a
report file could not be written.
.SH EXAMPLES
Preview this week's report without sending or moving the baseline:
.PP
.EX
sudo cti\-agent run\-domains \-\-dry\-run
sudo less /var/lib/cti\-agent/state/domains\-$(date \-u +%F).txt
.EE
.PP
Check DNS and mail only, printing the text report:
.PP
.EX
sudo cti\-agent cti\-domains \-\-no\-registrar \-\-no\-state\-write
.EE
.PP
Start a fresh baseline after changing resolvers:
.PP
.EX
sudo rm /var/lib/cti\-agent/state/domains\-state.json
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR run\-domains (1),
.BR cti\-mailer (1),
.BR cti\-agent (1)
.PP
RUNBOOK.md section 11g; fleet\-kit/README.md, "The weekly domains check".
